<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Operation Vulture, 1954</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The USAF at Dien Bien Phu, 29 April 1954.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Spring of 1954 found the Cold War quite cold.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Stalin has recently died and it is a mid-term election year for the Eisenhower administration with its tough on communism doctrines. In French Indochina, the ongoing catastrophe that is the siege of Dien Bien Phu is approaching its end game and the French government is desperately trying to get America involved to save the garrison.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;President Eisenhower is not keen on the idea but Admiral Arthur Radford, the Chairman of the Joint Chief’s of Staff (JCS) has discussed intervention employing strategic bombers and perhaps up to three nuclear weapons. In this reality, Congress has demanded that the USA demonstrate solidarity with France against the Communist Menace in southeast Asia, controlled as it is from a now leadership-deprived Moscow.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The assumption is that the Soviets will not intervene because there must be an ongoing&amp;nbsp;power struggle to fill the&amp;nbsp;void created by Stalin’s passing and the communist Chinese are still licking their wounds from the Korean War.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The time is right and massive air attacks on the Viet Minh forces in the hills and approaches to Dien Bien Phu will wreck Ho Chi Minh’s army and allow France to negotiate their way out of Indochina.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;This will prevent the Vietnamese domino from falling to communism.&amp;nbsp; What can possibly go wrong?&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Initially one plan called for some sixty &lt;EM&gt;B-29 &lt;/EM&gt;bombers from Guam and Japan to concentrate at Clark Air Force Base in the Philippines but Air Force Chief of Staff, General Nathan Twining has a new plan. The &lt;EM&gt;B-29&lt;/EM&gt; force is getting old and is outdated in virtually all respects while the cream of the bomber crews have been allocated to Strategic Air Command (SAC).&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Using&amp;nbsp;SAC and the huge &lt;EM&gt;B-36 Peacemaker&lt;/EM&gt; will allow far more bombs to be dropped and also demonstrate to the world the combat power&amp;nbsp;of SAC even without using&amp;nbsp;atomic weapons.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;CINCSAC, General Curtis LeMay is against taking any of the &lt;EM&gt;B-36&lt;/EM&gt; force off nuclear alert but Twining gets support of the rest of the Chiefs and of Congress.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;A reluctant President authorizes the action and gives LeMay a free hand to use one SAC combat wing plus whatever support he needs from the other services.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;You are Commander, 6th Bombardment Wing, Strategic Air Command based at Walker Air Force Base, near Roswell NM and have been ordered to&amp;nbsp;execute OPERATION VULTURE. Your command has been redeployed to Clark Field, P.I. and you have the conventional munitions required to destroy the communist forces besieging the French at some place called Dien Bien Phu.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;You have had your briefing directly from CINCSAC and he has decided that SAC will do the job alone.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The navy had offered an aircraft carrier battle group to provide fighter escort and flak suppression to and from the target area but the &lt;EM&gt;B-36&lt;/EM&gt; has to be able to operate unescorted.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; Besides, the bombers will be operating above any communist AAA.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;So the only role that the USN will play is in-route SAR in case of mechanical casualties.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;The Viet Minh have no air force and both the JCS and the State Department have confirmed that&amp;nbsp;probability of Chinese or Russian intervention is very low.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;You are entirely responsible for organization, target selection and loadouts for your sorties.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The French have advised that they will be conducting their regular, low altitude air operations with forces from Hanoi and the aircraft carrier &lt;EM&gt;Arromanches&lt;/EM&gt; in the Gulf of Tonkin throughout the hours of daylight on the 29th and 30th of April.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Scenario Designer's Notes:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Player’s caveat: please read before flaming.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;This scenario represents one possible permutation of events surrounding the last days&amp;nbsp;under siege of the French Union entrenched camp near the Laotian frontier; at the Seat of the Border County Prefecture - Dien Bien Phu (DBP), Tonkin, French Indochina.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;It presumes that the United States has decided to intervene to save the French forces and bomb the Viet Minh using conventional weapons, a plan designated in real life as OPERATION VULTURE.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The units available in Command’s CWDB at this time, do not permit an absolutely accurate rendering of the&amp;nbsp;historical OOB’s so representative equivalents have been used for the desired effect.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;In this&amp;nbsp;scenario &lt;EM&gt;F4U’s&lt;/EM&gt; have replaced the French &lt;EM&gt;F6F &lt;/EM&gt;and &lt;EM&gt;F8F&lt;/EM&gt; fighter-bombers based at Hanoi and on the carrier &lt;EM&gt;Arromanches&lt;/EM&gt; as the latter two types lack the range to carry a useful load to DBP and return. Since the loadouts used by the longer-legged &lt;EM&gt;Corsair&lt;/EM&gt; is essentially identical to those carried by the &lt;EM&gt;Hellcats&lt;/EM&gt; and &lt;EM&gt;Bearcats&lt;/EM&gt;, the real effect on game play and compromise of&amp;nbsp;the real capabilities of the combatants should be minimal. Likewise ground units and deployments have been selected to be representative where actual units and locations are irrelevant, conflicting or not available in the DB or the consulted historical record. The aim is to provide reasonable cause and effect for what is obviously a hypothetical situation.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;There are some inconsistencies in the references used to build this scenario.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; For example &lt;/SPAN&gt;Bernard Fall (author of &lt;EM&gt;Hell in a Very Small Place&lt;/EM&gt; - an essential read for anybody remotely interested in the real events) states that the French used &lt;EM&gt;B-26 Marauders&lt;/EM&gt; but photographic evidence from the battle clearly shows &lt;EM&gt;A-26 Intruders&lt;/EM&gt; in French air force colours operating over the entrenched camp.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Fall, who was there and often watched the planes depart Hanoi for the battle area is an otherwise impeccable witness but squaring this circle was pretty easy as the CWDB does not include the &lt;EM&gt;B-26&lt;/EM&gt;.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;I suspect that there may be an editing or translation error in the tabulated data of Appendix C to&amp;nbsp;Fall's book, or at least my well-worn first-English language edition.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;President Eisenhower was absolutely against US intervention to save the French but Vice-President Richard Nixon and JCS Chairman Adm Radford lobbied hard for VULTURE in some form.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; Ever the consumate politician, there may have been&amp;nbsp;an outside chance that&amp;nbsp;Ike may have given in to political pressure and authorised the operation but I would assess that the probability he would have&amp;nbsp;allowed nuclear weapons to be used is as close to zero as makes no difference. So, while s&lt;/SPAN&gt;everal sources repeat the plan to use up to three nuclear weapons against Viet Minh troops to break the siege, this CMANO version of VULTURE is entirely conventional.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; In this alternate reality &lt;/SPAN&gt;I have thrown SAC into the breach without support as it is well known that General LeMay did not really play well with the other services so the prospect of SAC alone or nothing may not be too farfetched.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;SAC is using the &lt;EM&gt;B-36&lt;/EM&gt; "&lt;EM&gt;Peacemaker&lt;/EM&gt;" because I have an odd soft-spot for this Brontosaurus of a strategic bomber that was already obsolete when the first one rolled off the production line.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;In the days before surface to air missiles, the SAC Bomber Barons were almost unanimous in their belief that bombers could operate at high altitudes alone and without escorts.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Besides, there are no communist air forces to intercept the &lt;EM&gt;B-36's&lt;/EM&gt;, right?&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;-C&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
